                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6ff40cb3-182e-3324-8949-6d9646924f5e",
                        "entry_id": "0921bb77-2c6c-33f1-9b40-76776141eb92",
                        "glosses": [
                            "element (required aspect or component of a cause of action) (also collective as “elements”)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "masculine",
                            "strong"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "81223c4a-99da-4b21-986c-114410972656",
                                "sense_id": "6ff40cb3-182e-3324-8949-6d9646924f5e",
                                "text": "Es entspricht weiter ständiger Rechtsprechung des BGH, dass § 548 BGB auch Ansprüche des Vermieters wegen Veränderungen und Verschlechterungen der vermieteten Sache erfaßt, die nicht auf Mietvertrag, sondern auf unerlaubte Handlung gem. § 823 ff. BGB gestützt sind. Würden konkurrierende Ansprüche nicht ebenfalls von § 548 BGB erfaßt, würde dessen Anwendungsbereich erheblich eingeschränkt. So findet § 548 BGB auch Anwendung auf Ansprüche, die sich auf demselben Sachverhalt begründen, jedoch aus Tatbeständen außerhalb des Mietrechts hergeleitet sind.",
                                "translation": "It is also established case law of the BGH that § 548 BGB also covers claims of the landlord for alterations to and deterioration of the rented property that are not based on the rental agreement but on tort pursuant to § 823 et seq. BGB. If competing claims were not also covered by § 548 BGB, its scope of application would be considerably restricted. § 548 BGB also applies to claims that are based on the same facts but are derived from elements outside of tenancy law.",
                                "english": "It is also established case law of the BGH that § 548 BGB also covers claims of the landlord for alterations to and deterioration of the rented property that are not based on the rental agreement but on tort pursuant to § 823 et seq. BGB. If competing claims were not also covered by § 548 BGB, its scope of application would be considerably restricted. § 548 BGB also applies to claims that are based on the same facts but are derived from elements outside of tenancy law."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
